{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/431172-beginning-prometheans-skills-and-outlook","id":431172,"title":"Beginning Prometheans skills and outlook","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-07T03:29:57-08:00","id":431172,"title":"Beginning Prometheans skills and outlook","content":"My DM wants to start with my characters creation, but also wants me to have all my skills in place, and a finished character sheet, which makes it hard for me to see some of the skills I will have.This is a solo game and I am playing a Curious Nepri who will not be explained what she is. I really wanted to make a character who had mental motivations, but not mental stats. She is equally fascinated with driving a car as how people react to lying. If anything, she is less interested in mental skills because it seems about studying the world rather than what humans do and why they do them.<br /> <br /> I really want her to be more physical and social (in a creepy way) and while I can always play off the body remembers physical gifts, I have some real trouble rping and understanding how to play off her lying and streetwise capabilities right out of the water. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> Finally, the Nepri mindset is hard to achieve with no others nearby. Phlegm is emotionless and calm, but that seems pretty bare to begin with. Without the superiority gig, its hard not to turn that into Melancholic by becoming introspective. I was thinking of making her emotionless but kind of driven. She needs more, needs to find out more, I even made her lustful to show a primal need for more knowledge and will put herself and others in harms way to achieve something intangible. If the DM decides that the story has room maybe dabble in Flux, if not she fluctuates between Gold and Iron. Any help in how to play a Nepri without any knowledge of their heritage and how they may become social?<br /> <br /> This is my first Promethean game. Been wanting to run one for a long time, but my players never seemed interested. When my fiance decided to run one with me I was excited, and hoping to smooth over any first game bumps this may have out the bat, as much as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5197-kadakithis","name":"kadakithis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T04:04:51-08:00","id":431212,"title":"","content":"Prometheans skills from the bat I always find personally a tough thing to justify. I myself have not played much Promethean, though I always figured they awoke to their existance as a blank slate and the skill dots represent muscle memory and things they have discovered before play starts. Physical dots are more simple then, as they can be represented as the relative state of the Promethean's body and natural skill. Social skill falls down to a developing personality... Also how well they can communicate, things like Empathy show how much a Promethean naturally gets other people.<br /> Mental skills should develop from how Intelligent the Promethean is to begin with, to analyse and learn from their surroundings. Going back to Social skills, anyone can lie. it's being convincing to the other person where alot of the skills come in. Think about just why someone would believe your character when they lie to them. Perhaps it's to do with their looks, how they talk or body language. Merits can help represent these kind of things too. You can justify Streetwise if your Promethean spends time in a rough neigbourhood or watches deals in the night, or they just naturally hold themselves as someone who knows their stuff, which probably fits your character better. I don't think many people question the stoic type that stands tall when they do speak. There is also some creepiness in pure stoicism, speaking only when neccessary.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}